{"The cached ID resolution in getForLogin calls session.identityProviders().getById(id) which routes back through the session to this same cache provider class, creating a recursive caching path - should use idpDelegate directly": 0.27604493498802185, "Cleanup references hardcoded \"alias\" instead of the actual IDP alias \"idp-alias-\" + i, meaning none of the 20 created IDPs will be cleaned up after the test and cleanup will fail trying to remove a non-existent IDP": 0.9020366668701172, "The isEnabled() re-check was added to the ORG_ONLY and ALL paths but not to the REALM_ONLY path (line 64), which also uses getForLogin and is subject to the same wrapping concern - incomplete fix": 0.9281558990478516, "Guard against a null identity provider before calling registerIDPLoginInvalidation - removing a non-existent alias will throw a NullPointerException": 0.8581628799438477, "In the remove method, registerIDPLoginInvalidation(storedIdp) uses the delegate-fetched model, but in the else branch the primary registerIDPInvalidation uses cached.getIdentityProvider() - these models can be out of sync and login cache invalidation should use the same model reference": 0.6004334092140198}